{
  "_readme": "Golden set for the Chalk next-session eval (PROD-85). Each item is a RecommenderInputs snapshot minus `candidates` — the runner fills those from every row of scripts/data/movements.csv (kettlebell and bodyweight) through the same toCandidates() the edge function uses. `expect` holds the deterministic bounds the runner asserts (max_duration_minutes, max_blocks, must_cover) plus `notes`, the coach's-eye description the LLM judge grades against. Categories: baseline (no signal at all), readiness (scales volume to how the lifter feels and how long they have), balance-target (must train the named overdue patterns), equipment (only prescribes loadable weights), goal (recognisable protocol flavour), history (adapts to what was just done or how long it has been), house-voice (never says 'debt').",
